---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="Pixel Lens collects no data. Here is exactly what the extension stores and why.">
  <article class="prose-docs mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Pixel Lens collects nothing.</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-400">Last updated: October 15, 2026</p>

    <h2>What the extension stores</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your preferences (color format, grid settings, toggles).</li>
      <li>Live CSS edits you make, keyed by page URL, so they can be re-applied when you come back.</li>
      <li>Agent bridge settings (on/off and port).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All of it lives in your browser's extension storage (<code>chrome.storage.local</code>) and never leaves your device. Uninstalling the
      extension deletes it.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There is no analytics, telemetry, crash reporting or tracking.</li>
      <li>There are no accounts and no remote servers.</li>
      <li>All code that runs ships inside the extension package; nothing is loaded from the network.</li>
      <li>It only runs on a tab after you invoke it there (opening the Pixel Lens tab in DevTools counts), and never reads pages in the background.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The agent bridge</h2>
    <p>
      If you turn on the agent bridge, the extension connects to an MCP server on your own computer at <code>127.0.0.1</code>. Data about the
      active tab (element styles, measurements, screenshots you or your agent request) is sent to that local server and from there to the AI
      client you configured. What that client does with it is governed by its own privacy policy. Turn the bridge off at any time from the
      options page.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This site is static HTML with no cookies and no analytics.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Open an issue on <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
